@verbs editor
@tier player
@title the editor: how a long text is written
@see mail boards configuration

Letters and notes on boards are written with your editor.

  editor
  editor <name>

With nothing, it tells you which editor you use and which ones you can
choose; with a name, you change it. It can also be changed from
'configuration'. It is kept with your account.

With the menu editor, the default one, you type the lines one after
another. A line with just ** takes you to the menu:

  I   insert lines before a line number
  D   delete lines: a number or a range like 1..3
  L   show the lines written
  M   change a text for another within some lines
  C   go on writing at the end
  S   quit and save the text
  Q   quit without saving the text
  H   show the help

The direct editor is the same, but ** saves the text straight away, and
the menu commands are used without leaving the text by typing ~ first:
~l shows the lines, ~q quits without saving.

The letters work in upper or lower case, and they are the same in both
editors.

If you are not sure how this works, do not change it: the menu editor
does everything and is the easiest one for a newcomer.
